    <description>The Board&apos;s Accommodation Request Form, offered inside every exam application. Shows the Board&apos;s confidentiality statement and records the accommodations requested on a Person Disability record, one per form: coming back to the step or resuming updates the same record, and answering No after Yes deletes it with its documentation item and file. When an accommodation is requested, it adds a required Documentation for Disability Related Needs checklist item (Exam Accommodations category) to the form&apos;s draft, once, and shows its upload (Subflow: Document Checklist Upload). Applicants must upload it before they continue; staff entering a paper application can leave it for later. The item moves to the application at Certify with the other documents. Runs in system context because the details field is encrypted and not open to portal users.</description>
    <dynamicChoiceSets>
        <name>choice_Accommodations</name>
        <dataType>Multipicklist</dataType>
        <displayField xsi:nil="true"/>
        <object xsi:nil="true"/>
        <picklistField>Accommodations__c</picklistField>
        <picklistObject>PersonDisability</picklistObject>
    </dynamicChoiceSets>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>forT_RequestId</name>
        <description>The request recorded on this form: the one found from earlier, or the one just created.</description>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>BLANKVALUE({!GetExistingRequest.Id}, {!CreateAccommodationRequest})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>forT_RequestName</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>LEFT(&quot;Accommodation request: &quot; &amp; {!varT_ExamName} &amp; &quot; examination&quot;, 80)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Subflow: Accommodation Request {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Subflow: Accommodation Request</label>
